From: wasm-dolphin patch snapshot <snapshot@local.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:01:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0069-web-input-backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The browser's ControllerInterface backend, ciface::Web (CIFACE_USE_WEB,
Emscripten only): four "Web/N/Wii Remote" devices whose state the page sets
through the exported SetWiimoteState (buttons word, pointer, Nunchuk stick,
optional motion). Their input names are the Bluetooth passthrough device's
(A, B, 1, 2, -, +, HOME, Up/Down/Left/Right, Nunchuk C/Z/X±/Y±, Accel *,
Gyro *) plus Cursor X±/Y± and Cursor Hidden for pointing and Shake buttons,
so the emulated Wii Remote binds to them with an ordinary WiimoteNew.ini and
upstream's IR camera, motion and extension emulation run unchanged.

